Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:30:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08/26] [Diffusion] Causal KV seam: recache capture archives
 only the written frames

A clean forward that re-materializes earlier frames in place (e.g. a LongLive
1.0 prompt-switch KV recache) is a separate capture kind:

* CausalKVRecache(window, written, epoch_id, cause, details): the window fed
  through the forward and the global token ranges the cache actually stored
  (a sink-protected recompute leaves the sink out).
* CausalKVCapture.kind ("clean_commit" | "kv_recache"); causal_kv_capture_scope
  accepts a chunk or a recache; CausalKVRun.end_recache(recache) commits.
* CausalDMDDenoisingStage._causal_kv_recache(...) builds the descriptor from
  frames; _causal_kv_recache_scope(run, recache) captures every CFG stream's
  recache forward run inside it (through _update_causal_context_cache) and
  calls end_recache once on success only. The backend archives exactly the
  written ranges as a new cache epoch, never the sink.
* Capture stays at the attention level (CausalWanSelfAttention.forward);
  attach_causal_kv_backend numbers the attention modules of the fully built
  DiT, so pipelines that re-class or replace transformer blocks after
  construction still capture every layer.

Tests: descriptor math and validation, capture kinds, every stream captured
then one commit, no commit after a failed recache, no-op without a run,
attach-time layer numbering.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
